  "observations": [
    "A nearest-food plus local-repulsion heuristic is a repeatable balance probe, not proof of human difficulty or optimal play. Targets are selected from the whole bounded local pool; this grants more awareness than an ordinary player viewport.",
    "Fish can only be eaten at or below 92% of player length. The 92–112% band behaves as harmless peers, so some slightly smaller fish intentionally remain inedible.",
    "The player physical length can jump when overlapping many prey in the same tick; single equal-ratio prey growth diminishes with scale. Rendering smoothness is outside this engine-only review.",
    "Dash exhaustion now locks further boosts. Holding boost through full energy recovery never retriggers dash; releasing at or above 24 energy clears the lock. This removes the former automatic recharge/boost pulses.",
    "All later-size population starts are fixtures and do not claim the newborn naturally reached 10/100/1000 cm."
  ],
